   ```go
   newEntry.Title = sanitize(newEntry.Title) // Implement a sanitize function to clean input
   ```
3. **Use Prepared Statements**: Always use prepared statements for SQL queries to prevent SQL injection attacks. Ensure that user inputs are never directly concatenated into SQL commands.
   ```go
   stmt, err := db.Prepare("INSERT INTO entries (id, title, content, lastModifiedBy, lastModifiedAt) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?)")
   ```
4. **Implement Authorization Checks**: Before allowing updates or deletions, verify that the user has permission to modify the specified entry. This prevents Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) vulnerabilities.
